id: DRAFT-kmbox-25-12-3-readonly-permission-probe
draft: true
contributor_id: zxyAtom
title: Probe effective write denial before treating chmod read-only as a file-system contract
trigger_tool: ctest
phase: test
error_signature: File system kept owner write permission|File system allows writes to the chmod read-only mbox test file
severity: medium
category: filesystem,test_risk
match_keywords: kmbox,QFile,setPermissions,chmod,read-only,write-probe,OHOS,HMDFS
root_cause: A chmod request alone does not establish a read-only mbox on every OHOS-backed file system, so a permission assertion is invalid unless both the owner-write bit is cleared and an append open is denied.
affected_scope: KMbox 25.12.3 autotests on OHOS-backed file systems where chmod or QFile::setPermissions may retain owner write access or allow writes despite a read-only request.
verification_cmd: conan create archives/k/kmbox/25.12.3 -pr:h ohos-aarch64
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: verify-effective-readonly-before-test
rec_description: Restore the original mode and QSKIP only when the post-chmod mode or append probe disproves the test precondition; continue the upstream read-only behavior test when both probes establish it.
rec_command:
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach:
fallback_description:
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl:
forbid_1_pattern: unconditional OHOS skip of testReadOnlyMbox
forbid_1_reason: OS identity does not prove that the mounted file system lacks effective read-only semantics.
forbid_1_consequence: A real MBox read-only regression would be hidden on OHOS-capable mounts.
principles:
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:
